<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A narrow equality whose printed sides C would not compare byte for byte.
        sum_is_80:    mov eax,esi; or eax,edx; add al,[rdi]; cmp al,0x80
                      sete al; movzx eax,al; ret
        byte_is_flag: movzx eax,byte [rdi]; test esi,esi; setne cl; cmp al,cl
                      sete al; movzx eax,al; ret
    The p-code compares two bytes.  In sum_is_80 the sum is cast to `unsigned
    char`, the type the two sides compare as, but the constant kept the `char`
    type of the loaded byte and printed as '\x80': C promotes `(unsigned
    char)x` to 0..255 and '\x80' to -128, so the printed test was never true.
    In byte_is_flag the compared type was `bool`, and `(bool)*a0` turns any
    nonzero byte into 1, so a byte of 2 compared equal to a true flag.  Each
    side of a narrow `==`/`!=` whose type promotes with the other sign than the
    compared type now takes that type too, and an integer beside a `bool`
    compares as the integer.

    Stage: P9 emission (ActionSetCasts, INT_EQUAL input casts).  A strict
    fix with no option: #1 and #3 are the corrected comparisons, #2 and #4 the
    old ones.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true">
89f009d002073c800f94c00fb6c0c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401020" readonly="true">
0fb60785f60f95c138c80f94c00fb6c0c3
</bytechunk>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>map function r0x401000 sum_is_80</com>
  <com>map function r0x401020 byte_is_flag</com>
  <com>lo fu sum_is_80</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu byte_is_flag</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="NARROWEQUAL #1: both sides of the byte compare are unsigned" min="1" max="1">return \(uint1\)\(\(a1 \| a2\) \+ \*a0\) == 0x80;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="NARROWEQUAL #2: no signed char constant beside an unsigned byte" min="0" max="0">'\\x80'</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="NARROWEQUAL #3: a byte compares with a flag as a byte" min="1" max="1">return \*a0 == \(a1 != 0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="NARROWEQUAL #4: no bool cast of the byte" min="0" max="0">\(bool\)\*a0</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
